<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Vanilla Psycasts Expanded rebalances: psyfocus and entropy costs raised on about a dozen psycasts, longer durations
		for Blade Focus and Firing Focus with a stronger Firing Focus, a weaker Protection damage reduction, a smaller
		Paralysis Pulse, a slower-casting and smaller Thunderbolt, a goodwill cost on Mind Control, thralls unable to do
		animal, artistic and intellectual work, and matching description updates. With VPE - Gravcaster, its enhanced
		gravity hediff also stops slowing movement.
		This folder only loads when VPE is active (see loadFolders.xml); the Gravcaster change is gated on its packageId.
		The mod gate sits on an <li> inside a sequence, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads MayRequire only on
		list elements.

		In the original this sat behind a Too Many Mods setting (TMM_VPE_PsycastRebalances, default on). The setting is
		dropped: this mod is the opt-in now. Tree-order changes that used to share the block were deleted beforehand.

		Verified against VPE 1.6 by evaluating every xpath against the combined defs: all 28 operations find their target
		and every replacement changes the value. Thunderbolt and Vortex replace their whole psycast extension but keep the
		upstream path, level, order and prerequisite, so only their costs move.
	-->
	<!--
		Two more VPE changes, previously ungated in the core:
		- Enchant Quality can target buildings, so built furniture and structures can be upgraded in place instead of
		  having to be minified first. Upstream sets canTargetBuildings false; vanilla's CanTarget accepts a building
		  before it reaches the item-only thingCategory check, so the flip is enough.
		- The melee Empire warlord (Empire_Caster_Warlord_Melee) spawns as a Warlord psycaster. Upstream VPE gives only
		  the ranged warlord a psycast extension, though both spawn in Empire raids at the same weight. Stat upgrade points
		  are 0~0, matching Too Many Mods' caster rebalance, where upstream's ranged warlord has 2~6.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
				<xpath>Defs/PawnKindDef[defName="Empire_Caster_Warlord_Melee"]</xpath>
				<value>
					<li Class="VanillaPsycastsExpanded.PawnKindAbilityExtension_Psycasts">
						<implantDef>VPE_PsycastAbilityImplant</implantDef>
						<initialLevel>1</initialLevel>
						<statUpgradePoints>0~0</statUpgradePoints>
						<unlockedPaths>
							<VPE_Warlord>1~4|2~12</VPE_Warlord>
						</unlockedPaths>
					</li>
				</value>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
